    "method": "Sentinel-2 composite renders at 3 km, 1 km and 400 m (RGB, NIR, SWIR, brightness, edge). Dales 1962 describes the citadel as built on a rock outcrop on the eastern edge of the Dasht River plain. South-east of the Dasht channel a dark red-brown patch about 110-120 m wide and 250-300 m long (dark in SWIR), centred near 25.4986 N 61.9503 E, stands out from the pale alluvium; we take it as the outcrop carrying the citadel. The Wikidata starting point lies about 80 m west of it."
